From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Emmanuel Gil Peyrot <linkmauve@linkmauve.fr>
Date: Sun, 14 Jan 2024 10:54:01 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] media: cedrus: Add JPEG decoding

Baseline 8-bit YCbCr JPEG up to 6144x6144, written by the rotate and
scale output as NV12; 4:2:2 and 4:4:4 come out as 4:2:0. Motion JPEG
too, whose frames may leave the Huffman tables out: the Annex K tables
stand in for them.

The engine parses the headers itself, so it takes no request, keeps a
CPU mapping of the coded buffer and drains as a stateful decoder.

Ported from Emmanuel Gil Peyrot's series to the reworked driver.
---
